{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation"},{"anchor":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"],"generated":true,"title":"Explanation"}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Design Principles","role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux’s surface area looks small — a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol — but the API is opinionated. These principles explain ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"why","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the API has the shape it does, so you can extend it correctly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"1. State is a value, observation is a class","anchor":"1-State-is-a-value-observation-is-a-class","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State is a struct. Mutations go through ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is predictable, snapshottable, and testable. SwiftUI observation needs an ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reference type. Reconciling these two requires a class that mirrors the struct.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" generates that class for you (","type":"text"},{"code":"<StructName>Observer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and wires up the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance that bridges the two. Don’t hand-write the observer. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"pack → reduce → unpack-diff → observe","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cycle is what gives you per-property re-renders without coupling reducers to a class.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" extends this to nested struct slices: each slice gets its own observer class so observation stays granular even across composition.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"2. Reducers are pure and synchronous","anchor":"2-Reducers-are-pure-and-synchronous","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers take ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Action","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", mutate state in place, and return an optional ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"reference"},{"text":". They never ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", never ","type":"text"},{"code":"throw","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and never call I\/O directly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Why: pure synchronous mutations are trivially testable, deterministic, and snapshot-friendly. When you need async work (network, disk, timers), return an effect — a ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" async closure that runs off the MainActor and dispatches follow-up actions back through ","type":"text"},{"code":"send","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"3. Effects run off MainActor; sends hop back","anchor":"3-Effects-run-off-MainActor-sends-hop-back","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"reference"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Sendable (Send) async -> Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs effects in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task { @concurrent in }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so they don’t block UI. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","type":"reference"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"@MainActor @Sendable (Action) -> Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so dispatching from inside an effect always lands back on MainActor — no manual hops, no race conditions on state.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The split is deliberate: effects own the work, the reducer owns the state.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"4. Persistence is invisible","anchor":"4-Persistence-is-invisible","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers mutate ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" properties; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" records every change in a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","type":"reference"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" debounces and drains those changesets through ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","type":"reference"},{"text":" closures.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You never write ","type":"text"},{"code":"db.save()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a feature. A reducer that adds an item is identical whether the entity is persisted to SwiftData, SQLite, or nowhere — register or don’t register a writer. This is the principle that makes Swidux apps feel small: persistence stops being a concern of feature code.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"5. Synchronous state, async persistence","anchor":"5-Synchronous-state-async-persistence","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State updates synchronously inside the reducer for instant UI feedback. Persistence happens asynchronously: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" change tracking is in-memory and free; the debounced persistence flush coalesces rapid mutations into a single batched write.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Tap-tap-tap-tap on an increment button updates the UI on every tap and produces one DB write a moment later. Reducers stay synchronous; storage stays cheap.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"6. Plugins are the single extension point","anchor":"6-Plugins-are-the-single-extension-point","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Everything that hangs off the dispatch cycle is a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":". Persistence, undo, killswitch, parental gate, paywall — same protocol, same lifecycle hooks. You can add your own without forking Swidux.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two structural patterns:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Core middleware","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") — action-agnostic. Doesn’t know your action type. Couples only to state shape ("},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for undo; "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" keypaths for persistence)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Domain plugins","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"KillswitchPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"ParentalGatePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", your own) — owns a state slice and an action enum. Wires into your root types via keypath + action lifter + extractor."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The decision rule: ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"does this need to know your action type?","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" If no, write core middleware and use ","type":"text"},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". If yes, write a domain plugin and use ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"7. Bind to the store, not to `@State`","anchor":"7-Bind-to-the-store-not-to-State","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Form inputs read from the store and dispatch on write. Use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" for the common case (read one property, dispatch one action), and fall back to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Binding(get:set:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the read is a transformation (optional unwraps, derived values) or the setter wraps the dispatch in animation or branching. Don’t buffer mutable form state in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and write back on a button.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Why: every mutation flows through the reducer, which means undo\/redo, persistence, and any plugin that watches the dispatch cycle sees every keystroke (subject to coalescing). If you stash state in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", those plugins are blind to it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The trade-off is more dispatches per keystroke. Coalescing — see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" — collapses bursts of the same action into a single undo step.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"8. Registration order matters at the boundaries","anchor":"8-Registration-order-matters-at-the-boundaries","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" snapshots in ","type":"text"},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so it must run ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" any plugin or reducer mutates state — register it first. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" drains changelogs in "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so it wants the post-mutation state — register it after undo. Domain plugins use only ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so their relative order rarely matters.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The recommended order:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. snapshots first","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. drains after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. domain plugins","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)","plugins.register(parentalGatePlugin)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"9. Strict concurrency, on purpose","anchor":"9-Strict-concurrency-on-purpose","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux is built for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swiftLanguageMode(.v6)"},{"type":"text","text":" and assumes Swift 6 strict concurrency throughout. State must be "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"text":". The macros mark generated code carefully. Effects use explicit isolation (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"@concurrent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is friction at first — you’ll get warnings about ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" types. Honour them. The result is a state-management layer that composes safely with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async\/await"},{"type":"text","text":" and SwiftData without the surprise data races you get from pre-Swift 6 designs."}]},{"text":"10. The store is opinionated; your app is not","anchor":"10-The-store-is-opinionated-your-app-is-not","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux gives you a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol, and three optional plugins. It does not give you:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A dependency-injection container (write your own "},{"code":"AppEnvironment","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A navigation library (use SwiftUI navigation).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A network layer (use ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSession","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", structured concurrency, or whatever you want).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An opinion on database (SwiftData, GRDB, SQLite, Core Data — register a "},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and Swidux doesn’t care).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The store owns one job: take an action, produce a new state, run effects. Everything else is yours.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Anti-patterns","text":"Anti-patterns","type":"heading","level":2},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"try","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" inside a reducer — return an effect instead.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Hand-writing the observer class when you could use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"db.save()"},{"type":"text","text":" from inside a reducer — use "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Mutating state from inside an effect — effects dispatch actions; the reducer mutates."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Owning the store with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@StateObject"},{"type":"text","text":" — use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ObservableObject"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Buffering form state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" and committing on submit — bind to the store directly."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Registering "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" before "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — snapshot must precede mutation."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples"]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/StateWriter":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/statewriter","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","abstract":[{"text":"Accumulates entity snapshots and produces batched async persistence work.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateWriter"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateWriter"}],"title":"StateWriter","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","role":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","kind":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux","role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"title":"Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Send":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/send","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Send","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Send","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A function for dispatching actions back to the store from within an effect."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","kind":"symbol","title":"Send"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","abstract":[{"text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Effect"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/binding(_:sending:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding"},{"type":"text","text":" that reads a property through the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"observer tree and dispatches an action when written."}],"title":"binding(_:sending:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"binding","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"KeyPath","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7KeyPathC"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"State","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Observer","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux0A10ObservableP8ObserverQa"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sending","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Binding","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI7BindingV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","conformance":{"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}]},"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/binding(_:sending:)"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingYourFirstApp":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingyourfirstapp","abstract":[{"text":"Build a counter app from scratch and meet the four moving parts of a Swidux project: state, action, reducer, and store.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Build Your First Swidux App","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Plugin Architecture","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","abstract":[{"text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"title":"UndoPlugin","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ChangeSet":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/changeset","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","abstract":[{"text":"Tracks which entity IDs have been created\/updated or deleted.","type":"text"}],"title":"ChangeSet"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every mutation for downstream persistence.","type":"text"}],"title":"EntityStore","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle.","type":"text"}],"title":"SwiduxPlugin","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","abstract":[{"text":"Coalescing persistence plugin.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","role":"symbol"}}}